A||||9||SCCA FIERO||My Coupe is now a fastback||||1||
Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||03-12-2000||08:44 PM||||Today I finshed installing the clip on my 88 Coupe. The clip was the exact same color as my car with perfect sail windows, the tail lights are perfect too. I like the way it looks now. My Fiero has an identity crisis. It's a Fastback V6 Coupe with GT wheels? The deck lid has a luggage rack on it, but I think it looks better than a spoiler on this car. I may get the luggag rack removed if I ever get it painted.<P>What I have done to my 88 Fiero:<BR>Installed a 2.8 V6 from an 86SE<BR>Installed a fastback clip from 86GT<BR>Installed 120 speedo, rally gauges<BR>GT steering wheel<BR>Shortened shifter<BR>Ported exhaust manifolds<BR>Holley scoop<BR>Black GT wheels (also have a set of 16" Centerline wheels with 225/50ZR tires)<BR>Poly dogbone bushings<BR>Installing front poly this coming weekend<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ozzy||03-12-2000||09:13 PM||||Right Arm dude!<P>Hey, my search has begun for a v6 Fiero to do the same type of thing to my '88 Coupe.<P>I checked out this 85GT yesterday but the kid that rebuilt the engine is somewhat flakey, so I don't really trust his work. The car had lots of stuff wrong with it as well. Got my eye on an 86 SE 4 spd in reportedly good condition and priced right. Will check it out on my way thru Oregon next week.<P>Do you have any pics on your web site of the car yet??<P>Ozzy||||reg||10
Z||000002||Shiner||03-12-2000||10:31 PM||||Now I know why I can't find body parts for the restoration of my '87 GT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||03-12-2000||11:02 PM||||I took pictures of the swap, but it was today and I haven't had time to get the pictures developed and scanned. I will get them up soon.<P>Shiner, what parts do you need? I have almost another fastback clip minus the grills and 1 tail light.<P>I keep looking at it and it looks better and better every time I look at it. Is it possible to be obsessed with a car? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||03-13-2000||09:16 AM||||Hey SCCA, could you post a pic for us?  I'm having trouble envisioning the fastback body with the 88 Coupe nose & tail and no "ground effects" on the sides.  But I bet it looks great...nice and clean.||||reg||1
